==Strategy==
This stage is fairly intimidating, with Infernal Tyrant Nyandam supported most of the time by endless problematic peons. Fortunately, all those peons have very low health. Not to mention, 8 Zollows spawn throughout the stage which could more or less defeat your stronger units in the frontline. Money management is not too much of a problem here, as the peons, especially Sir Seals, will provide you with rather large amounts of money. Despite the large amount of damage Infernal Tyrant Nyandam does, he has multiple large blind spots, which ensures not all your cats are destroyed whenever he attacks, though those within the range of his first attack will most certainly be defeated.

For the strategy, use cheaper units with high movement speed and damage to reach the frontline within seconds like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], Talented [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]/[[Cutter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Neo Cutter Cat]]. Don't bother bringing tanks if they do not have the [[Survive]] ability, instead, 1-2 meatshields like [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] or [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] should be sufficient to permanently stall the boss. Do not try to bring crowd-controlling units as Infernal Tyrant Nyandam is [[Immune to Weaken]], [[Immune to Knockback|Knockback]] and [[Immune to Surge|Surge]], meaning that the only way to knock him back is by brute force or the [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper]] item.

